                <pb facs="0620" n="608" xml:id="pg608"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.6511/110: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-01T20:00:00-03:00">June 1, 1940—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:09 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>242. President Vargas is delighted with news in the Department’s telegram 147,
                    May 31, 5 p.m. He tells me that he will send a commission to the United States
                    very soon to proceed with the business.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
